1
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,647
Automatic reports holds three weekly reports, ready for the staff meeting.

2
00:00:09,647 --> 00:00:15,935
Load & availability: each player’s load ratio and load over the last four weeks…

3
00:00:15,935 --> 00:00:21,106
…then who was unavailable, and for how many days and matches.

4
00:00:21,106 --> 00:00:29,705
The team report puts check-in response, fatigue, mood and load ratio in one table, with the change since last week.

5
00:00:29,706 --> 00:00:37,963
Switch to 4 or 12 weeks for a longer view. Any report opens in the Explorer to dig further.

6
00:00:37,963 --> 00:00:47,024
The player report follows one player: fatigue, sleep, load ratio and minutes over the last days.

7
00:00:47,024 --> 00:00:56,214
Attendance, under Tracking, shows who attended which event over any period.

8
00:00:56,214 --> 00:01:02,511
One row per player, one column per event — with each player’s attendance rate.

9
00:01:02,511 --> 00:01:08,838
Export it as a CSV, or send it to your inbox for the club.
